WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:01.687
&gt;&gt; Shocking news.

00:00:01.687 --> 00:00:02.981
Just kidding, not shocking at all.

00:00:02.981 --> 00:00:05.374
A new study finds that
raising the minimum wage,

00:00:05.374 --> 00:00:07.094
a sort of reasonable amount relative to

00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:09.631
the cost of living, has economic benefits

00:00:09.631 --> 00:00:11.791
and generally improves people's lives.

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:13.030
Many right-wingers will tell you

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.120
that if you raise the minimum wage,

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.141
especially to $15 an hour,
as many Democrats want to do,

00:00:19.141 --> 00:00:20.230
it'll be the Apocalypse.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:24.201
Businesses will close,
widespread unemployment.

00:00:24.201 --> 00:00:26.904
Unfortunately, the facts
don't really bear that out.

00:00:26.904 --> 00:00:29.191
We have a new study
conducted by UC Berkeley

00:00:29.191 --> 00:00:30.306
which proves the opposite.

00:00:30.306 --> 00:00:32.118
They looked at Seattle, Washington,

00:00:32.118 --> 00:00:34.754
and they looked at
Seattle's $15 minimum wage,

00:00:34.754 --> 00:00:36.571
and it worked really, really well.

00:00:36.571 --> 00:00:39.786
The study used the rest
of Washington's economy

00:00:39.786 --> 00:00:42.706
as a sort of control to predict
what would have happened

00:00:42.706 --> 00:00:44.877
in Seattle if they had not increased

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.596
the minimum wage to $15.

00:00:46.596 --> 00:00:48.513
On January 1st of this year,

00:00:48.513 --> 00:00:50.914
the $15 minimum wage took effect,

00:00:50.914 --> 00:00:53.442
and now unemployment
is lower than it's been

00:00:53.442 --> 00:00:56.350
in Seattle for nearly a decade.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.554
In Seattle, wages are up,

00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:00.210
unemployment is down,

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.612
and the number of hours worked is up,

00:01:02.612 --> 00:01:05.051
meaning that employers
aren't cutting hours

00:01:05.051 --> 00:01:07.034
to account for the higher minimum wage.

00:01:07.034 --> 00:01:10.119
This was even true in
the restaurant industry,

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:11.991
even at fast food restaurants,

00:01:11.991 --> 00:01:14.302
which is a common example from the right.

00:01:14.302 --> 00:01:16.670
The conservatives like to say,

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:17.575
when you raise the minimum wage,

00:01:17.575 --> 00:01:20.312
it's particularly bad for
fast food restaurants,

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.470
and the truth is, people
weren't being laid off

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:24.605
in the way Republicans said would happen.

00:01:24.605 --> 00:01:26.888
The higher minimum wage drew people

00:01:26.888 --> 00:01:29.553
to those fast food jobs, not away,

00:01:29.553 --> 00:01:33.098
and those workers are
also able to themselves,

00:01:33.098 --> 00:01:35.276
as a result of earning a higher salary,

00:01:35.276 --> 00:01:36.913
have a higher standard of living.

00:01:36.913 --> 00:01:39.035
These are meaningful trends.

00:01:39.035 --> 00:01:41.497
The data here is really impactful.

00:01:41.497 --> 00:01:43.186
Because Seattle didn't just suddenly

00:01:43.186 --> 00:01:45.162
raise its minimum wage six months ago,

00:01:45.162 --> 00:01:46.801
they've been slowly and steadily

00:01:46.801 --> 00:01:49.222
raising it over the last several years

00:01:49.222 --> 00:01:53.025
up to $15 per hour at the
beginning of this year,

00:01:53.025 --> 00:01:55.522
and things have been
progressively getting better

00:01:55.522 --> 00:01:58.031
and better since the
beginning of these increases.

00:01:58.031 --> 00:02:01.115
The study found that instead
of the new minimum wage

00:02:01.115 --> 00:02:03.506
making it harder for businesses to find

00:02:03.506 --> 00:02:05.726
what are called low-skill employees,

00:02:05.726 --> 00:02:07.737
it's causing surrounding communities

00:02:07.737 --> 00:02:10.034
to raise their wages to compete with

00:02:10.034 --> 00:02:12.237
the new opportunities in Seattle.

00:02:12.237 --> 00:02:14.379
Companies are struggling when they're not

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:16.424
paying their workers enough instead of

00:02:16.424 --> 00:02:17.306
the other way around.

00:02:17.306 --> 00:02:19.121
You hear, oh, if minimum wage goes up,

00:02:19.121 --> 00:02:20.642
that will make companies struggle.

00:02:20.642 --> 00:02:22.181
No, the companies not paying

00:02:22.181 --> 00:02:23.949
the higher wages are struggling.

00:02:23.949 --> 00:02:25.788
And some of this is pretty intuitive.

00:02:25.788 --> 00:02:28.118
If people have more money to spend,

00:02:28.118 --> 00:02:29.963
because the minimum wage went up,

00:02:29.963 --> 00:02:32.922
that will help businesses,
including fast food.

00:02:32.922 --> 00:02:35.421
Since people earning in that range

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.630
are more likely to go to fast
food restaurants as well.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.807
And more and more people are working,

00:02:40.807 --> 00:02:44.115
they're working more hours,
they're getting paid more,

00:02:44.115 --> 00:02:46.355
all of which stimulates the economy.

00:02:46.355 --> 00:02:48.950
Seattle is the first major city

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.439
to raise its minimum wage in this way,

00:02:51.439 --> 00:02:52.982
and this is now going to become

00:02:52.982 --> 00:02:54.992
part of a larger study at Berkeley

00:02:54.992 --> 00:02:57.358
to look at other cities
raising their minimum wages.

00:02:57.358 --> 00:02:58.522
This is very good news.

00:02:58.522 --> 00:03:00.347
&gt;&gt; Right, and conservatives
have this talking point

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:02.137
that if you raise the minimum wage,

00:03:02.137 --> 00:03:03.485
then you have to make up for it

00:03:03.485 --> 00:03:06.961
by lowering hours, or
cutting staff in some way,

00:03:06.961 --> 00:03:09.153
as if there's no other factors there.

00:03:09.153 --> 00:03:12.001
And I understand that a company may

00:03:12.001 --> 00:03:14.648
budget out a certain
amount to labor costs,

00:03:14.648 --> 00:03:16.661
but there's other things
in that pie chart.

00:03:16.661 --> 00:03:18.292
Like, for example, corporate profits,

00:03:18.292 --> 00:03:19.443
and when you're talking
about big companies

00:03:19.443 --> 00:03:21.238
like McDonald's or Walmart,

00:03:21.238 --> 00:03:22.698
they can easily afford to do that.

00:03:22.698 --> 00:03:24.156
&gt;&gt; No doubt about it.

00:03:24.156 --> 00:03:26.439
It is not a linear relationship.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.189
If you raise wages X,

00:03:29.655 --> 00:03:31.769
you don't have to raise all prices

00:03:31.769 --> 00:03:33.759
that exact same percentage.

00:03:33.759 --> 00:03:35.975
And by the way, there's
another really common

00:03:35.975 --> 00:03:38.253
conservative talking point

00:03:38.253 --> 00:03:40.282
from those who try to
debunk the minimum wage,

00:03:40.282 --> 00:03:43.257
which is listen, if
$15 is better than $12,

00:03:43.257 --> 00:03:45.316
and more money for everybody is good,

00:03:45.316 --> 00:03:48.941
why not make the minimum
wage $200 an hour,

00:03:48.941 --> 00:03:50.584
and then everything would be great?

00:03:50.584 --> 00:03:51.417
See?

00:03:51.417 --> 00:03:52.675
You couldn't, so you shouldn't raise

00:03:52.675 --> 00:03:54.386
the minimum wage at all.

00:03:54.386 --> 00:03:55.669
No one is asking for that.

00:03:55.669 --> 00:03:57.274
That is a total red herring.

00:03:57.274 --> 00:03:59.676
That is not an equilibrium wage,

00:03:59.676 --> 00:04:02.581
given the cost of
living, and productivity,

00:04:02.581 --> 00:04:04.132
and what you need to make in order to have

00:04:04.132 --> 00:04:05.372
a livable wage.

00:04:05.372 --> 00:04:08.086
There's no economic argument

00:04:08.086 --> 00:04:09.982
for a $200 an hour minimum wage.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:12.957
Just because $15 is better than $12,

00:04:12.957 --> 00:04:15.547
or maybe $18 would be better than $15,

00:04:15.547 --> 00:04:17.885
it doesn't mean that any serious people

00:04:17.885 --> 00:04:20.073
are calling for a $200 minimum wage,

00:04:20.073 --> 00:04:22.226
so please, do not fall for that

00:04:22.226 --> 00:04:23.656
when right wingers say that if

00:04:23.656 --> 00:04:24.899
raising the minimum wage is good,

00:04:24.899 --> 00:04:26.451
just keep on raising it.

00:04:26.451 --> 00:04:28.396
It's not a serious economic argument

00:04:28.396 --> 00:04:29.324
that anybody is making.

